 If you don't take this extra step in your Roth IRA, you're going to mess up your retirement

2
00:00:04,460 --> 00:00:09,140
 because a lot of us didn't learn about money in school. We often get our financial literacy

3
00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:14,560
 from social media accounts or worse from dangerous online forums. What a lot of people don't tell you

4
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:19,640
 is that you can't just put money into a Roth IRA. You have to invest it. If you just put money

5
00:00:19,640 --> 00:00:24,680
 into a Roth IRA, your money does not grow. If you think about it, a lot of these people want you to

6
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:29,240
 put your money into their companies. And if you don't invest your money, these companies are going

7
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:34,160
 to use your money to invest for themselves instead. And you'd be surprised by how many

8
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:39,480
 people are not investing their money. Because just by maxing out your Roth IRA for the next 40 years

9
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:45,760
 and not investing it, you would only have around $280,000. But if you invested it into a low-cost

10
00:00:45,760 --> 00:00:51,760
 index fund that tracks the S&P 500, you would have around $3 million. Let that sink in.

